 lnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prototype Fund Switzerland 2026-27: Responsible and Susta
 inable AI
DESCRIPTION:Since 2020 the Prototype Fund Switzerland has strengthened the 
 common good with open-source\, public-interest technology\, supporting int
 erdisciplinary teams to develop and test early-stage projects that show ho
 w open source\, data and digital technologies such as AI can create real s
 ocietal value. The 2026-2027 edition focuses on Responsible and Sustainabl
 e AI: building the path toward a more responsible and sustainable AI\, tec
 h and digitalization landscape\, open source and beyond. THIS YEAR'S FOCUS
 : projects that reduce resource use\, energy consumption or emissions\; st
 rengthen accountability\, transparency and governance\; and contribute to 
 resilient and trustworthy digital systems\, including sustainable digitali
 zation and digital sufficiency\, public-interest AI and data infrastructur
 es\, and tools for governance\, oversight or digital sovereignty. PUBLIC I
 NTEREST TECH areas span sustainability and climate\, participation and civ
 ic tech\, education and literacy\, health and inclusion\, and open knowled
 ge and data. WHO THEY FUND: individuals and small teams open to open sourc
 e\, AI and iterative experimentation\, eager to combine technical capabili
 ty with societal and political awareness\, willing to share learnings\, mo
 tivated to work on pressing societal problems through technology\, with an
  early-stage but well-thought-out concept\, and eligible to work in Switze
 rland. SUPPORT: up to CHF 50\,000 in funding\, a 4-month prototyping phase
 \, coaching\, mentoring and workshops\, and access to a strong network acr
 oss tech\, policy and society. Teams are strongly encouraged (though not r
 equired) to publish code\, data or components under open-source licenses a
 nd to document their approach. TIMELINE: applications 21 July to 7 Septemb
 er 2026\; rolling jury selection August-September 2026\; prototyping mid-O
 ctober 2026 to mid-February 2027\; outputs and learnings November 2026 to 
 July 2027. Questions: info@prototypefund.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Prototype Fu
 nd Switzerland (Opendata.ch)\nLocation: Switzerland\; applicants must be e
 ligible to work in Switzerland.\nAward: Up to CHF 50\,000 per project\, pl
 us coaching\, mentoring and workshops and access to a tech/policy/society 
 network. No application fee.\nDuration: 4-month prototyping phase (mid-Oct
 ober 2026 to mid-February 2027)\n\nMore: https://prototypefund.opendata.ch
 /en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prototypefund.opendata.ch/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland\; applicants must be eligible to work in Switzerland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eth-ai-center-fellowships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: ETH AI Center Doctoral and Postdoctoral Fellowships 2027
DESCRIPTION:The ETH AI Center's flagship fellowship programme funds doctora
 l and postdoctoral researchers doing interdisciplinary AI research\, eithe
 r within AI foundations or between AI foundations and application areas\, 
 including safe and trustworthy AI. Fellows are co-supervised across ETH gr
 oups and join the AI Center's community. ELIGIBILITY: doctoral track needs
  a Master's in computer science\, machine learning\, statistics\, physics\
 , engineering\, applied mathematics or a related field\, completed by June
  2027\; postdoc track needs a PhD completed by June 2027. Two to three ref
 erence letters are required. Selection weighs research excellence\, interd
 isciplinary collaboration and impact orientation. APPLICATION: separate po
 rtals for the doctoral and postdoc tracks (linked from the programme page)
 \; deadline 27 October 2026 at 16:00 CET. Related CLS and ELLIS PhD tracks
  have their own applications.\n\nOrganisation: ETH AI Center\, ETH Zurich\
 nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.\nAward: Doctoral
  fellowship: CHF 73\,100 (year 1)\, CHF 78\,300 (year 2)\, CHF 83\,500 (ye
 ar 3). Postdoc fellowship: CHF 92\,500 (year 1)\, CHF 97\,200 (year 2). No
  application fee.\nDuration: About 3 years (doctoral\, extendable by up to
  1 year) or 2 years (postdoc)\, starting around September 2027.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:traces-art-science-energypolis-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: TRACES Art & Science @ Energypolis 2027: residency at the
  EPFL Laboratory for Energy Materials (Sion)
DESCRIPTION:TRACES is a new art and science residency run by the Foundation
  for the Sustainable Development of Mountain Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Vala
 is-Wallis\, Energypolis\, the City of Sion and the Canton of Valais. The 2
 027 pilot embeds one visual artist for three months in Prof. Sascha Feldma
 nn's Laboratory for Energy Materials at EPFL\, which works on light-matter
  interactions and soft semiconductors for flexible solar cells\, energy-ef
 ficient screens and emerging quantum technologies. The artist develops ori
 ginal work in dialogue with the lab around the energy transition and the m
 aterials of the future\, with studio and production space\, scientific men
 toring and a public final presentation on 15 April 2027. ELIGIBILITY: conf
 irmed\, professional international visual artists aged 25 or over who fini
 shed their studies at least two years ago and have at least two years of p
 rofessional practice\; applications in English or French with a letter of 
 intent (two A4 pages)\, portfolio and CV via the online form. Laureate sel
 ected 7 December 2026. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026\, 23:59 Swiss time (CET)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Foundation for the Sustainable Development of Mountain 
 Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Valais-Wallis\nLocation: Energypolis campus\, Sio
 n\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.\nAward: Artist stipend of CHF 2\,000 
 per month (CHF 6\,000 total) covering living and research costs\, housing 
 in Sion\, travel from home and back up to CHF 1\,500\, and a separate prod
 uction budget set by the curator. No application fee.\nDuration: Three mon
 ths\, 11 January to 18 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.traces-opencall.ch
 /en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.traces-opencall.ch/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Energypolis campus\, Sion\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
